---
description: Team workflow and safety rules for the Incident Zero hackathon repo
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` in the repo root before making any change. It is binding. For Incident Zero work, AGENTS.md names `docs/hackathon/RULES.md`, `TEAM_CONTEXT.md`, `FEATURES.md` and `ISSUES.md` as the rules, context, backlog and issue board.

Non-negotiables:
- One ISSUES.md entry → one branch (`feat|fix|docs|test|chore/<NN>-<slug>`) → one PR. Never commit or push to `main`.
- Plan first (files, interfaces, tests), then code only within the issue's scope.
- Read every file before editing it. Never invent APIs, endpoints, packages, config keys, or test output.
- Write tests, run the full suite and lint, and do one real run (live demo or offline bundle). Never skip or weaken tests.
- Hackathon rules: agent changes the system only via the Action API after explicit human approval; never read feature-flag (flagd) settings to diagnose; never modify the demo, faultctl, or scoring harness; never invent evidence.
- Never merge or approve PRs yourself.
